if-addrs lists interfaces' addresses with getifaddrs on Radix as on the
other POSIX systems (ADR 0336). Radix has no netlink, so the change
notifier, which waits on a NETLINK_ROUTE socket, is left out as on the
BSDs; and mlibc's struct ifaddrs has ifa_broadaddr and ifa_dstaddr
apart, not in a union as glibc's, so a broadcast address is read from
ifa_broadaddr.

